{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>First time</b><br>Leaning. Clinging, and so in the language of Kedar [and it has no parallel in Scripture]:" "חבלתך. Like (הנה) יחבל און (he will conceive trouble), and it is from חבלי יולדה (birth pangs):" "<b>Second time</b><br>Her beloved awakened her and said to her: Who is this coming up from the desert? — whom her [first] beloved sought, just as I did, and I awakened you under the apple tree under which we were lying, to remind you that there your mother conceived you. And the matter is because she conceived under the apple tree, therefore its scent resembles the scent of the apple:" "<b>Third time</b><br>Who is this coming up. Then the nations of the world will say this concerning the congregation of Israel when she comes up from the desert of the peoples with the Messiah:" "And she said to him: under the apple tree I awakened you. And the sense is: I awakened you with my speech and my prayers, which gave birth to you, in the manner of what is said: תפוחי זהב במשכיות כסף דבר דבור על אפניו (apples of gold in settings of silver, a word spoken upon its face):"], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:45:03.461167326Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}